# `[hidethis]` — hide from live / production

Use this **exact** token including square brackets: **`[hidethis]`** (lowercase, no spaces inside brackets).

The repo includes a **production-only** Vite transform (`vite/strip-hidethis-plugin.ts`) that removes marked regions from built JS/TS — they **remain visible in `vite dev`** so you can draft in place.

## Forms

### 1. Rest of line (most common)

Put **`[hidethis]`** immediately before the text you want removed from the **live** site. Everything from **`[hidethis]`** through the **end of that line** is stripped in production builds.

```tsx
<p className="text-sm text-forest-600">
  Guests see this sentence only.
  [hidethis] Internal note: verify VAT copy with accountant before launch.
</p>
```

After production build, the paragraph contains only the first sentence (the plugin removes ` [hidethis] Internal note…`).

### 2. Multiline block

For larger hidden chunks, wrap between **`[hidethis]`** and **`[endhidethis]`** on their own lines (or inline block in source — the regex is non-greedy).

**In `.tsx`, prefer JSX comments** so the file stays valid — the build strips the whole `{/* … */}` … `{/* … */}` range:

```tsx
<div>
  {/* [hidethis] */}
  <section>
    <p>Draft content stripped from production bundles.</p>
  </section>
  {/* [endhidethis] */}
</div>
```

Plain markers without JSX comments also work in non-JSX contexts:

```tsx
<section>
  <h2>Public heading</h2>
  [hidethis]
  <p>Draft paragraph only for staging review.</p>
  [endhidethis]
</section>
```

The entire block including markers is removed in production.

**Order of stripping:** JSX-wrapped blocks first, then generic `[hidethis]…[endhidethis]`, then rest-of-line patterns.

## Rules for agents & contributors

1. **Spelling / casing:** Only **`[hidethis]`** and **`[endhidethis]`** are recognized (exact strings).
2. **Do not** put `[hidethis]` inside runtime strings you need in production logic (e.g. `const msg = "[hidethis]..."`) — the build will delete those segments and may break code. Use markers in **JSX markup / adjacent text** or refactor to env-based copy.
3. **Markdown / docs:** Same markers work in `.md` **only if** those files are processed through the same transform (default plugin targets imported `.ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx`). Raw markdown not bundled is **not** stripped — use CMS flags or remove manually for published docs.
4. **SSR / server bundles:** If SSR is added later, extend the plugin or duplicate stripping for server entrypoints.

## Verification

- **Dev:** `npm run dev` — you should still see `[hidethis]` content.
- **Prod bundle:** `npm run build` then search the output `dist` assets for `[hidethis]` — it should not appear.

## Related implementation

- Plugin: `vite/strip-hidethis-plugin.ts` (imported from `vite.config.ts`).
- Toggle behaviour is **`config.isProduction`** during `vite build` only.
